    "intro_html":  "Bangers and mash is British pub food at its most honest: sausages, buttery mashed potatoes, peas, and an onion gravy poured over the whole thing. The sausages got the nickname because wartime versions had so much water in them they burst in the pan. Ours do not, and this plate carries 39 grams of protein for about $2.83 (at everyday cost).",
