    "cost_closing_html":  "About \u003cstrong\u003e$2.83 a bowl\u003c/strong\u003e (at everyday cost) for a full pub plate with gravy. Potatoes and onions are the two cheapest staples on the board, which is exactly why this dish survived a century of hard times.",
    "shop_smart":  [
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eSausages are the entire budget here.\u003c/strong\u003e Everything else on the list barely moves the needle. Buy them on sale, freeze them, and the cost of this recipe drops hard.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eBuy potatoes in the big bag.\u003c/strong\u003e This uses a serious amount of them for the mash, and bagged potatoes cost roughly half what loose ones do per pound.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eFrozen peas are the right peas.\u003c/strong\u003e They are picked and frozen at peak, they cost less than fresh, and they need nothing but a minute of heat.",
                       "\u003cstrong\u003eThe gravy is butter, flour, onions and broth.\u003c/strong\u003e A splash of soy sauce is the trick that gives it the dark color and savory depth people assume comes from a packet."
                   ],
    "make_it":  [
                    "Weigh your empty mixing pot and write the number down for portioning later.",
                    "Peel and chunk the potatoes and get them going in salted water. Slice the onions thin and mince the garlic.",
                    "Heat the vegetable oil in a large skillet and brown the bratwurst slowly on all sides. Low and slow keeps the casings from splitting.",
                    "Move the sausages to a plate and start the gravy in the same pan, melting most of the butter and cooking the sliced onions until they go deep golden and sweet.",
                    "Add the garlic, then sprinkle in the flour and stir for a minute before streaming in the chicken broth while whisking.",
                    "Add the soy sauce and simmer the gravy until it thickens and coats a spoon, then season with salt and black pepper.",
                    "Drain the potatoes, mash them with the remaining butter, salt and pepper, and keep them loose enough to portion easily.",
                    "Warm the peas through, slice the sausages into thick coins, and combine everything with the gravy in your big pot."
                ],
